1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,480
If every cable on your elevator

2
00:00:01,490 --> 00:00:03,360
snapped at once, you'd fall about

3
00:00:03,370 --> 00:00:04,100
five feet.

4
00:00:04,154 --> 00:00:06,184
It's Monday morning, and Gus steps

5
00:00:06,194 --> 00:00:07,604
into the elevator on the twentieth

6
00:00:07,614 --> 00:00:09,054
floor, with his neighbor.

7
00:00:09,098 --> 00:00:10,988
Above them, six steel ropes hold

8
00:00:10,998 --> 00:00:12,278
the car, and any one of

9
00:00:12,288 --> 00:00:13,828
them could carry it fully packed.

10
00:00:13,872 --> 00:00:15,492
The neighbor has a plan anyway.

11
00:00:15,772 --> 00:00:17,272
If they ever snap, just jump

12
00:00:17,282 --> 00:00:18,192
at the last second.

13
00:00:18,246 --> 00:00:19,276
Gus does the math.

14
00:00:19,496 --> 00:00:20,986
A fall from the twentieth floor

15
00:00:20,996 --> 00:00:22,566
ends at seventy six miles an

16
00:00:22,576 --> 00:00:23,046
hour.

17
00:00:23,276 --> 00:00:24,706
His best jump is six.

18
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:26,180
And right then, all six ropes

19
00:00:26,190 --> 00:00:26,550
snap.

20
00:00:26,594 --> 00:00:27,424
The car drops.

21
00:00:27,434 --> 00:00:28,274
Gus floats.

22
00:00:28,284 --> 00:00:30,004
The neighbor gets ready to jump.

23
00:00:30,058 --> 00:00:31,578
And one second later, the car

24
00:00:31,588 --> 00:00:32,378
just stops.

25
00:00:32,432 --> 00:00:32,982
But wait.

26
00:00:33,092 --> 00:00:34,532
Nothing holds the car up.

27
00:00:34,542 --> 00:00:35,542
So why did it stop?

28
00:00:35,586 --> 00:00:37,046
You see, a little wheel spins

29
00:00:37,056 --> 00:00:38,526
as fast as the car moves.

30
00:00:38,776 --> 00:00:40,216
Spin it too fast, and its

31
00:00:40,226 --> 00:00:41,546
weights fly out and trip a

32
00:00:41,556 --> 00:00:41,886
brake.

33
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,310
Ever yanked a seat belt?

34
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:44,800
Pull it slowly, and it runs.

35
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:46,230
Yank it, and it locks.

36
00:00:46,284 --> 00:00:47,944
The brake is two steel wedges

37
00:00:47,954 --> 00:00:48,674
under the car.

38
00:00:49,004 --> 00:00:50,594
They jam against its rails, and

39
00:00:50,604 --> 00:00:52,214
the harder the car pulls, the

40
00:00:52,224 --> 00:00:53,094
harder they bite.

41
00:00:53,148 --> 00:00:54,898
Luckily, they need no power, no

42
00:00:54,908 --> 00:00:56,178
computer, and no luck.

43
00:00:56,232 --> 00:00:58,012
Unluckily, they only let go when

44
00:00:58,022 --> 00:00:59,362
somebody lifts the car.

45
00:00:59,406 --> 00:01:00,726
So the cables snapped, and Gus

46
00:01:00,736 --> 00:01:01,696
fell five feet.

47
00:01:01,916 --> 00:01:02,606
He's fine.

48
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:04,190
He's just stuck between floors,

49
00:01:04,310 --> 00:01:05,530
with a neighbor who still wants

50
00:01:05,540 --> 00:01:06,260
to jump.
